Collect C++ constructors and destructors with collect2 on mips-ecoff, as
GCC does on the other ECOFF MIPS targets, Ultrix and OSF/1. Without it the
compiler only marks each in a stabs set, __CTOR_LIST__, which nothing on
ECOFF gathers, so libgcc's empty list is used and global constructors
never run. collect2 instead runs nm on the linked program, writes a table
of the _GLOBAL_$I$ and _GLOBAL_$D$ functions it finds, and links again,
and __main runs them. Only the C++ toolchain is built with this.

--- a/gcc/configure
+++ b/gcc/configure
@@ -4925,6 +4925,7 @@
 			tm_file="${tm_file} dbx.h"
 		fi
 		tmake_file=mips/t-ecoff
+		use_collect2=yes
 		;;
 	mips-*-ecoff*)
 		tm_file="gofast.h mips/ecoff.h"
@@ -4932,6 +4933,7 @@
 			tm_file="${tm_file} dbx.h"
 		fi
 		tmake_file=mips/t-ecoff
+		use_collect2=yes
 		;;
 	mipsel-*-elf*)
 		tm_file="mips/elfl.h libgloss.h"
